    "body": "## Problem\n\nWhen a global statusline is enabled, horizontal split separators are internally marked as statuslines for mouse-resize handling.\n\nAs a result, clicking a column with a statusline click handler while the pointer is on a separator incorrectly dispatches that handler. The callback consumes the pending drag, preventing the separator from resizing the split.\n\n## Solution\n\nOnly dispatch statusline click handlers when the mouse is over an actual window-local or global statusline.\n\nKeep the internal statusline marker on split separators so that dragging them continues to resize the split correctly.\n\nFixes #42572",
    "closed_at": null,
